### Day 8/50 — Constraints

Not every value belongs everywhere.

A database has rules.

Some fields cannot be empty.
Some values must be unique.
Some things simply aren't allowed.

These are called **constraints**.

At first, rules can feel restrictive.

But without them,
data can become invalid,
inconsistent,
or completely messy.

Maybe boundaries work the same way.
They don't always stop things from happening.
Sometimes,

**They stop the wrong things
from entering places where they don't belong.**
